{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"45246929f529e7885396de70717efbc89f97997c7ce2402f0e6a9404661ebb05","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar reconciler status-mapping tests","key_entities":["_DRIFT_WARNED","outbound_mapper.reset_drift_warnings()","resolve_outbound_status","test_unmapped_status_drifts","test_status_mapping.py","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/outbound_mapper.py"],"problem_keywords":["test isolation","autouse fixture","process-global state","test ordering","shared mutable state"],"propositions":["Status-mapping tests share a process-global dedupe set _DRIFT_WARNED that is never reset between tests, causing test order-dependency when asserting drift warnings.","test_unmapped_status_drifts can fail if an earlier test records 'blocked' in _DRIFT_WARNED, suppressing the expected stderr warning.","An autouse fixture calling outbound_mapper.reset_drift_warnings() before each test isolates state and eliminates test ordering sensitivity.","The test module must add an oracle that is RED without the fixture (prior test's record suppresses warning) and GREEN with it (fixture clears set between tests)."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787648143556684865,"uuid":"cff1fcdc-ca2a-4784-8b97-cf73ec538776"}